4. PHASE TWO: GEMINI API INTEGRATION

Integrate WaveGuide AI with the official Google Gemini API.

Use the official Google Gen AI SDK for JavaScript and TypeScript when compatible with the existing application.

Use a current, supported Gemini model appropriate for conversational assistance, response quality, latency, and cost.

Inspect current model availability and select a valid model identifier.

Do not blindly hardcode an obsolete or unsupported model name.

Keep model selection configurable through server-side configuration where appropriate.

API integration requirements

- Send user messages to Gemini through a secure server-side endpoint.
- Keep the Gemini API key on the server.
- Never expose the API key in client-side JavaScript.
- Never use a NEXT_PUBLIC_ environment variable for the Gemini API key.
- Validate incoming messages.
- Handle model errors safely.
- Handle rate limits and timeouts.
- Limit the amount of conversation history sent with each request.
- Prevent excessively large prompts.
- Return predictable response structures.
- Provide meaningful loading and error states.
- Avoid logging full private conversations unnecessarily.

Use the existing backend architecture.

For a Next.js application, use an appropriate server-side route handler or server action, depending on the existing implementation.

If the project uses another framework, use its equivalent server-side mechanism.

Environment configuration

Use the appropriate server-side environment variable, such as:

GEMINI_API_KEY=

If the selected SDK or deployment environment uses a different supported variable name, document it and apply it consistently.

Add the variable name to the example environment file without inserting a real key.

Document how to configure the real key in:

1. Local development.
2. Google AI Studio, if applicable.
3. Vercel production environment settings.

Do not commit the real key to GitHub.

Do not print the key in logs.

Do not claim the API is connected until a real request has succeeded.

Official documentation

Use the official Gemini API documentation as the technical reference:

https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs

https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/api-key

Follow current SDK and API guidance instead of relying on outdated examples.

