11. PHASE NINE: STREAMING RESPONSES

Where supported by the selected Gemini API and application architecture, implement streaming responses.

The objective is to display text as it is generated rather than forcing the customer to wait for the entire response.

Requirements:

- Use a supported streaming API.
- Return chunks through an appropriate transport.
- Handle aborted requests.
- Handle connection interruptions.
- Stop generation when a supported cancellation request is received.
- Prevent duplicate messages when retries occur.
- Avoid leaving the interface permanently loading.
- Do not expose provider-specific internal errors.
- Clean up streams when the conversation component is unmounted.

If streaming cannot be implemented safely in the current architecture, implement reliable non-streaming responses first and document the limitation.

Do not simulate streaming by revealing a completed response one character at a time.

